@startuml sequence-judges-ask
!include elvira.iuml
' What: an extractor's question either comes back as a banded Verdict or passes through unjudged and counted; the job never fails because of a judge.
' Kind: UML sequence diagram, one Panel.ask call. Scope: inside one worker process; the catalog call that stores the region is left out.
' Source: issue evilflowers-worker#6; evilflowers-knowledge Cookbooks/Deploy-Decision-Models (2026-11-16)

title One judged proposal: Panel.ask (evilflowers-worker#6, 2026-11-16)

participant "extractor job\n(e.g. image figures)" as job
participant "Panel\n(per job)" as panel <<focus>>
participant "Budget" as budget
participant "CircuitBreaker\n(per client)" as breaker
participant "DeciderClient\n(decider-vision)" as client
participant "decider-vision\n(shared, app01)" as model <<proposed>>

job -> panel : ask(decider_vision, FIGURE_KIND, state, [crop])
alt no client (judges off, no URL)
  panel --> job : None (outcome=disabled)
else budget spent
  panel -> budget : allows()?
  panel --> job : None (outcome=budget)
else breaker open
  panel -> breaker : allow()?
  panel --> job : None (outcome=open)
else call
  panel -> client : ask(question, state, images, timeout=min(timeout, budget left))
  client -[$accent_msg()]> model : <b>POST /v1/systemone</b>\nstate, images (base64), questions
  alt 200 with an answer
    model --> client : answers.kind {choice, probabilities}, model
    client --> panel : Verdict(verdict, p, model, revision)
    panel -> breaker : success()
    panel -> panel : band from judge_thresholds[question]
    panel --> job : Verdict(band=keep | review | hide | None)
  else timeout, connection error, 5xx, 429
    client --> panel : JudgeUnavailable
    panel -> breaker : failure()
    panel --> job : None (outcome=unreachable)
  else 4xx / unparseable answer
    client --> panel : JudgeRefused / JudgeInvalid
    panel -> breaker : success() (the service is up)
    panel --> job : None (outcome=refused | invalid)
  end
  panel -> budget : spend(elapsed)
end

caption Every path counts <service>_judge_total{question,outcome,band}; a call also records <service>_judge_seconds.\nA None means "post the region without a band, as today".
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · evilflowers-worker · docs/diagrams/sequence-judges-ask.puml
@enduml
